course: dictionary
lesson: 6446
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which one is meant by looking at the words around it. This is context, and it is one of your best tools for reading.
explain: «In Liverpool, Reece lives with his nan in a small house.» Nan here means grandmother, because a child lives with a grandma, and the sentence is about a home and family. Ask yourself: which meaning of the word fits this sentence?
explain: The same word can also name bread. «Pass the nan, please» at a curry meal means a soft flat bread, not a grandma. The place and the food are your clues. In computers, NaN is short for "not a number", an error value, and it has nothing to do with family or food.
fact: Nan is an informal word for grandmother, used in the UK, Australia, New Zealand and Ireland.
fact: Nan is also spelt nana or nanna, and naan is a soft flat bread from South Asia.
fact: «NaN» in computers means "not a number", an error value.
fact: In the USA, children more often say grandma or granny.
fact: Phrases you may hear: my nan, at my nan's, nan bread.
exercise: «In Liverpool, Reece lives with his nan in a small house.» What is his nan? | A soft flat bread | *A grandmother | A teacher at his school | A type of house
exercise: Asha asks at a curry meal, «Pass the nan, please!» What is the nan? | *A soft flat bread from South Asia | A grandmother | A hug | A computer error
exercise: A computer shows NaN in a cell. What does NaN mean? | A grandmother | *Not a number, an error value | Nothing at all, it is empty | A soft flat bread
test: «I'm going to my nan's for tea.» Which meaning of nan fits? | Not a number | *Grandmother | Soft flat bread | Error value
test: Which word is another spelling of the word for grandma? | nap | *nana | naan | NaN
exam: «A palindrome reads the same forwards and backwards, such as mum, dad, Nan, level and noon.» What is a palindrome? | A soft flat bread | *A word that reads the same both ways | A computer error | A word for a grandmother
